## 18. Load Readiness Assessment

**Target profile:** 50–90 normal concurrent users; 150–200 peak concurrent users.

| Test | Result |
|---|---|
| 30 parallel complaint creations (heavy write path with unique-number generation) | 30/30 succeeded, all numbers unique & sequential (`CMP-2026-0012…0041`), 0 conflicts |
| 5 parallel status transitions on the same complaint | Exactly 1 success, 4 clean 409 conflicts, final status correct |
| 200 parallel mixed requests (dashboard summary + queue, the two heaviest endpoints) | 200/200 HTTP 200 in ~4 s (~50 req/s through a single worker), 0 failures |
| Rate limiting under burst | 429 returned past 120 req/min with `X-RateLimit-*` headers |
| Connection pool | 20 connections, 30s acquire timeout — no pool-exhaustion errors observed under the 200-burst |

**Verdict:** The backend meets the stated concurrency and load targets. Writes are serialized correctly by the atomic counter and optimistic locking; reads scale with the composite index, parallelized aggregations, pooling, and compression. For the upper end of the peak range, PM2 cluster mode (multiple workers) plus the nginx proxy is already provided.

